# Laragon local development

Decided by Bambie on 9 November 2026 (#213). Laragon is the only supported local set-up. This repository is its own Laragon project: Apache with PHP 8.4 (NTS build) through FastCGI (mod_fcgid), MySQL 8.4 and Node 22, with the values in `docs/laragon/profile.json`. Never suggest containers, virtual machines or any other local server stack, and never use `php artisan serve`.

## Before any development work: the live preview gate

Run this at the start of any development or coding work (code, tests, docs, config, installs or commits), after every branch switch, and before moving to another repository:

1. **Load the latest version and updates.** `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\preview.ps1`. It stops if tracked files are uncommitted, fetches, fast-forwards the branch, merges `origin/main` into it (never a rebase), runs `composer install` or `npm ci` when a lock file changed, and reports pending migrations. Ask before running migrations. When none are pending, it syncs roles and permissions as a deploy does (the seeders in `deploy/cloudron/activate-release.sh`).
2. **Start Laragon.** The same script checks that Laragon, Apache and MySQL are running, that `/healthz` shows the checked-out revision on PHP 8.4 through FastCGI (`php_sapi` is `cgi-fcgi`), and starts Vite on port 5174 if nothing listens there. Starting Laragon, clicking Reload or switching its profile or PHP version needs Bambie's click in Laragon: ask her with AskQuestion.
3. **Open it in Cursor's browser.** Open <http://apes-intranet.test>, confirm it loaded, report the URL, the Vite port and a screenshot, then say "Preview ready, starting work". Call `SetActiveBranch` after a branch change.
4. **If it won't load after two attempts, stop.** Report the blocker and ask how to proceed before doing any work.

Exit code 3 from the script means a decision (uncommitted changes, a diverged branch, a merge conflict): ask with AskQuestion. Exit code 1 is a blocker: report its message.

## Preview and FastCGI

- The live preview is <http://apes-intranet.test>, served by Laragon's Apache from `public/` through the junction `C:\laragon\www\apes-intranet`. Vite hot reload is on port 5174. Mail goes to `storage/logs/laravel.log`.
- Laragon runs the NTS PHP through FastCGI (`C:\laragon\etc\apache2\fcgid.conf`), with separate PHP processes per site, so another project's `.env` cannot leak into this one. Never switch it back to the thread-safe build (mod_php).
- Keep `public/.htaccess` safe under FastCGI: no `php_value` or `php_flag` outside `<IfModule php_module>` (put local equivalents in `public/.user.ini`), and keep the `HTTP_AUTHORIZATION` rewrite rule. A test checks both.
- If the site is missing, run `scripts/laragon-setup.ps1 -NoDemo`. It only touches this project.

## Commands

Start each PowerShell session from the repository root with Laragon's NTS PHP 8.4, Composer and Node first on `PATH`, so the command line uses the same PHP build and `php.ini` as the website:

```powershell
$env:Path = 'C:\laragon\bin\php\php-8.4.27-1-nts-Win32-vs17-x64;C:\laragon\bin\composer;C:\laragon\bin\nodejs\node-v22;' + $env:Path; $env:XDEBUG_MODE = 'off'
```

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Live preview gate | `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\preview.ps1` |
| Set up or repair | `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\laragon-setup.ps1` |
| Load the demo data | `php artisan demo:seed` (or `composer demo:seed`) |
| Reset and reload the demo data | `php artisan demo:reset` (or `composer demo:reset`) |
| Vite hot reload | `npm run dev` (or `composer dev`) |
| Tests | `php artisan test` |
| Pint | `php vendor/bin/pint` |
| Larastan | `php vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --memory-limit=1G` |
| Accessibility check | `$env:BASE_URL = 'http://apes-intranet.test'; $env:A11Y_BROWSER_CHANNEL = 'msedge'; npm run test:a11y` |

- Use Laragon's newest NTS PHP 8.4 (`C:\laragon\bin\php\php-8.4.*-nts-*`), as on Cloudron. The Cloudron release build (`deploy/cloudron/deploy.ps1`) uses PHP 8.4 too, and stops if the PHP is not 8.4.
- Test against the demo data. Sign in as any role with the QA role switcher at <http://apes-intranet.test/qa> (fake `qa-<role>@example.test` accounts, no password). See `docs/laragon/demo-data.md`.
- `composer install` and `npm ci` may run without asking when `vendor/` or `node_modules/` is missing or a lock file changed. Ask before migrations, `demo:reset` (it empties the local database), or any system tool install.
- Fake data only in the local database. See `docs/local-development.md` for the full guide.
